  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on minimizing the probability of a loss, defined as the chance of receiving 0 Euros. The individual’s deliberation indirectly acknowledges this by highlighting that B has 'only a positive outcome,' which implies avoidance of any outcome that is not positive (i.e., 0 Euros). While the individual does not explicitly calculate or refer to probabilities of loss, their reasoning aligns with the core logic of the decision reason: preferring the option with no risk of a zero (loss) outcome. The information considered (presence of a positive, certain outcome) overlaps with the relevant information for the decision reason (probability of loss). The justification (choosing B because it avoids any non-positive result) matches the rule of the reason (prefer the lottery with lower probability of loss). Although the reasoning is expressed in simpler, qualitative terms, it reflects the same underlying principle. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this decision reason, albeit implicitly.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
